        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Mao Zedong</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1893 CE – 1976 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">26 December 1893, near Shaoshan village in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hunan">Hunan</a>, under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a>; son of Mao Yichang, a formerly impoverished peasant who had become one of Shaoshan's wealthiest farmers, and Wen Qimei</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">9 September 1976, shortly after midnight, aged 82, after years of lung and heart ailments and three heart attacks that year</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Founding member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-communist-party">Chinese Communist Party</a> (1921); Chairman of the Military Commission (from 1935); Chairman of the Communist Party (from 1943); paramount leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a> (1949-1976) and its President until 1959</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/long-march">Long March</a>; founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>; land reform and the campaigns against 'counter-revolutionaries'; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-leap-forward">Great Leap Forward</a> and the famine that followed; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cultural-revolution">Cultural Revolution</a>; Mao Zedong Thought and the theory of people's war; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung">Little Red Book</a>; poetry and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calligraphy">calligraphy</a></span></div>
